  "text": "The error 'upstream connect error or disconnect/reset before headers. reset reason: overflow' is produced by the following chain:\n\n1. **Reset reason string** (`envoy--v1.31.2` `source/common/http/utility.cc`): The function `Utility::resetReasonToString` maps `Http::StreamResetReason::Overflow` to the string `\"overflow\"` (line 1031).\n\n2. **Error message assembly** (`envoy--v1.31.2` `source/common/router/router.cc`): `Filter::onUpstreamReset` assembles the full error body using `absl::StrCat(\"upstream connect error or disconnect/reset before headers. \", ..., \"reset reason: \", Http::Utility::resetReasonToString(reset_reason), ...)` and sends it downstream.\n\n3. **Overflow trigger — pending requests** (`envoy--v1.31.2` `source/common/conn_pool/conn_pool_base.cc`): In `ConnPoolImplBase::newStream`, when there is no ready connection, the pool checks `host_->cluster().resourceManager(priority_).pendingRequests().canCreate()`. If the pending request circuit breaker limit is exceeded, it calls `onPoolFailure(..., ConnectionPool::PoolFailureReason::Overflow, ...)` and increments `upstream_rq_pending_overflow_` (lines 282–287).\n\n4. **Overflow trigger — max streams per connection** (`envoy--v1.31.2` `source/common/conn_pool/conn_pool_base.cc`): In `ConnPoolImplBase::attachStreamToClient`, when a ready connection exists but max concurrent requests (streams) are exceeded (`resourceManager(priority_).requests().canCreate()` returns false), it similarly fires `onPoolFailure(..., ConnectionPool::PoolFailureReason::Overflow, ...)` and increments `upstream_rq_pending_overflow_` (lines 175–180).\n\n5. **Max connections overflow** (`envoy--v1.31.2` `source/common/conn_pool/conn_pool_base.cc`): In `ConnPoolImplBase::tryCreateNewConnection`, when `host_->canCreateConnection(priority_)` returns false (max_connections circuit breaker reached), it increments `upstream_cx_overflow_` (line 138).\n\n6. **Circuit breaker configuration** (`data-plane-api--84e84367` `envoy/config/cluster/v3/circuit_breaker.proto`): The `CircuitBreakers.Thresholds` message defines `max_connections` (field 2, default 1024) and `max_pending_requests` (field 3, default 1024) as `google.protobuf.UInt32Value` fields that control when the overflow condition is triggered."
